- op: discuss  # 2fcf
  at: '2026-08-02T20:49:18Z'  # 2fcf
  by: agent  # 2fcf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2fcf
  clock: 21  # 2fcf
  nonce: 2fcf  # 2fcf
  message: "FRESH-SUBSTRATE RE-MEASUREMENT 2026-08-02, after WI-zazul. STAYS VIOLATED, and\nthe root cause is now known to be at least TWO mechanisms rather than one.\n\nMETHOD, stated because the last two measurements in this investigation were\nnearly wrong for instrument reasons. True A/B on identical inputs: the same 9\nrepos at the same checkouts (/tmp/f5_cohort_pool plus repos/alertmanager and\nrepos/kserve), the same generic.claims.yaml, the same runner with only the\noutput directory changed. An instrument check asserting BOTH directions of the\nfix (os/chaos -> False, java.lang.System/System -> True) ran before any\nmeasurement and would have aborted the run. Compared with INV-karud's own\nrealizability probe, not a metric invented for the occasion.\n\nPOSITIVE CONTROL (L9): 114 of the 321 before-arm flows have an AMBIGUOUS\nshort-name sink, so the disambiguation path is genuinely exercised and a clean\nresult would have meant something.\n\nRESULT\n    flows            321 -> 312\n    ambiguous-sink   114 -> 111\n    NON-REALIZABLE    51 ->  43        (-8, and 0 flows ADDED)\n\nThe -8 is exactly WI-zazul's substring class, removed and nothing else:\nnet/http/httptest.NewRequest (2), net/http/fcgi.Get (2), defusedcsv.writer (2),\nnet.Close (1), otlptracegrpc.NewClient (1).\n\nTHE 43 SURVIVORS ARE A DIFFERENT DEFECT (filed as WI-damir, P1):\n  30  the emitted module slot holds a FILE PATH, not a module -- go\n      logging.go/Log (18), js iframeResizer.contentWindow.js/warn (8), js\n      d3.v6.js/log, js d3-dispatch.v2.js/get, js lib/application.js/debug,\n      python generate-versions-from-gomod.py/run.\n  13  go net/http/Do, where the match is CORRECT (the catalog entry is\n      net/http.Client and Client.Do does perform network IO) but the emitted\n      module records the package while the catalog records package.Type, so no\n      consumer can verify it by lookup. Labelling, not a wrong match.\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S OWN EVIDENCE. Its two headline examples were d3's\n`log` (the LOGARITHM reported as a console.log sink) and\nnet/http/httptest.NewRequest, and both were attributed to substring module\nmatching. Only httptest was. d3's `log` IS STILL PRESENT: `console` never\nsubstring-matched a file path, and that flow is matched through the\nno-module-hint path (gate_named_entry + ambiguous_names) rather than through\n_module_matches at all. A scope-axis error (L1) -- every count real, the\ngeneralisation to one mechanism wrong.\n\nWHAT WOULD MOVE THIS ITEM: WI-damir. Until the module slot carries a module,\nthe realizability of a sink cannot be checked by lookup at all, which is what\nthis invariant asserts. Do NOT close on the -8; that is a partition of the\nviolation, not its resolution (L14)."  # 2fcf
- op: discuss  # b28c
  at: '2026-08-03T01:17:24Z'  # b28c
  by: agent  # b28c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b28c
  clock: 22  # b28c
  nonce: b28c  # b28c
  message: "CORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S OWN EVIDENCE, 2026-08-02 (second such correction).\nStatus unchanged: still violated. Deliberately NOT re-scoped and NOT proposed\nas a refined-criterion closure -- see the last paragraph.\n\n(1) The 2026-03-26 entry is false in both halves. It says \"DDG-backed taint\npropagation now available\" and \"Realizability: significantly improved for\nPython and Rust functions with DDG data\". Measured today:\n\n  - For RUST: the rust def/use extractor has never had a production caller.\n    The sole call site passed the literal \"python\". Independently, rust.yaml\n    does not declare atomic_statement, so the CFG bottoms out at leaf tokens\n    and the extractor would emit zero edges even if it were invoked.\n  - For PYTHON and every other language: propagate_taint_ddg cannot remove a\n    flow at all. It builds ddg_forward (taint.py:1584-1587) and tainted_at\n    (1651/1658) and reads neither; the DDG selects only the confidence label.\n\nSo clause (a) has not been \"significantly improved\" by DDG for any language.\nIt has never been affected by DDG at all. Filed as its own invariant plus a\nsection 3a implementation item; NOT folded into this one, because this item is\nabout realizability of REPORTED PATHS (the sink-matching family: WI-zazul,\nWI-damir) while that one is about a specified mechanism not existing. Folding\nthem would repeat the scope-axis error this item's history was just corrected\nfor (L1); a work item can be done while its umbrella stays violated on a\ndifferent mechanism (L14 partition).\n\n(2) The 2026-08-02 verdict \"Clause (c) is UPHELD\" rested on the INV-javam\nunsupported-language disclosure, which is a DIFFERENT property -- it discloses\nlanguages with no taint catalog, not that structural results are labeled\napproximate. Clause (c) as literally stated is satisfied only by coincidence:\nverify_claims.py:853 hardcodes the string \"approximate\" into the message, and\n_flow_evidence_dict omits confidence and analysis_method entirely, so the\nlabel a finding actually carries reaches no consumer. A hardcoded constant that\nhappens to read correctly is not evidence that a property holds.\n\n(3) Clause (b) -- sanitizers on the path must actually neutralize the taint\ncategory -- remains unmeasured by any cohort in twelve discussion entries.\nNote it is not unimplemented: sanitizers do prune the BFS walk. What has never\nbeen tested is whether the neutralization is correct. Worth splitting into its\nown item rather than riding along unverified.\n\nWHY NOT A REFINED-CRITERION CLOSURE. The standing pattern (INV-fahub,\nINV-numat, INV-pubom, D13) refines an acceptance property OVER VERIFIED\nEVIDENCE where the literal invariant is unmet for an understood, accepted\nreason. Here the opposite holds: the mechanism turned out LARGER than filed and\nthis item's own evidence OVERSTATED what was measured. Refining now would\nratify a measurement error."  # b28c
- op: discuss  # 21d1
  at: '2026-08-03T04:38:23Z'  # 21d1
  by: agent  # 21d1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 21d1
  clock: 23  # 21d1
  nonce: 21d1  # 21d1
  message: "CLAUSE (b) MEASURED, 2026-08-03 — first time since this item was filed\n2026-03-25. Twelve prior discussion entries carried it as neither claimed nor\ntested; it is now tested.\n\nCLAUSE (b): \"sanitizers on the path must actually neutralize the taint\ncategory in question.\"\n\nMETHOD. Three arms, identical fixture, only the path differing. Positive\ncontrol FIRST, because a \"confirmed\" verdict proves nothing unless the\nunsanitized arm is provably violated.\n\n  A  source -> sink, no sanitizer                       violated   (control)\n  B  source -> MATCHING sanitizer -> sink               confirmed  (neutralised)\n  C  source -> NON-MATCHING sanitizer -> sink           violated   (correctly not)\n\nArm C is the load-bearing one. The matching sanitizer is plaintext ->\nciphertext; the non-matching one is key_material -> derived_key, sitting in\nexactly the same path position. Only the category-matching barrier\nneutralises, which is precisely what the clause asserts. Without arm C, arm B\nwould only show that \"some sanitizer on the path clears the flow\".\n\nVERDICT ON CLAUSE (b): the mechanism is CORRECT, with three scope limits that\nmust travel with any closure and are filed separately:\n\n 1. SAME-FUNCTION SANITISATION IS NOT HONOURED. The barrier check exempts the\n    seed function, so encrypt-then-write inside one function reports a false\n    violation. Measured: all-three-in-one-function -> 1 finding; sanitiser on\n    an intermediate hop -> 0. This is a common real-world shape.\n 2. THE BUILT-IN VOCABULARY IS CRYPTO-ONLY. 12 sanitizer entries across 5\n    languages, all plaintext->ciphertext or key_material->derived_key. No\n    escaping, quoting, parameterised-query or path-normalisation sanitiser\n    exists, so clause (b) is verified for ONE taint-category family and is\n    unmeasurable for the rest -- a scope disclosure, not a pass.\n 3. THE BUILT-IN PYTHON ENTRIES ARE UNREACHABLE. All four python plaintext\n    sources and all four python sanitizers are Class.method, and the analyzer\n    emits NO call edge for a chained method call. The shipped catalog cannot\n    exercise this clause on python at all; the measurement required declaring\n    project-local module-level functions.\n\nSo the honest statement is: clause (b) HOLDS for cross-function, category-\nmatched sanitisation within the crypto family, and cannot currently be\nexercised at all through the shipped python catalog."  # 21d1
- op: update  # 012f
  at: '2026-08-03T04:46:49Z'  # 012f
  by: agent  # 012f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 012f
  clock: 24  # 012f
  nonce: 012f  # 012f
  set:  # 012f
    fields:  # 012f
      statement: "For each taint source-to-sink path reported by the taint analyzer:\n\n(a1) ATTRIBUTION SOUNDNESS. Every reported flow must be verifiable from the\nemitted record alone. The sink's emitted module slot must hold a module --\nnot a file path, not an unresolved placeholder -- and the matched catalog\nentry's declared module must travel with the finding, so a reader can confirm\nthe match by lookup without re-running the matcher.\n\n(a2) DATA-FLOW CONSISTENCY WHERE COVERED. For any flow whose source and sink\ncall sites lie in the same function AND whose function has data-dependence\ncoverage, a reaching-definition chain must exist from the variable the source\ndefines to a use at the sink call site.\n\n(a3) PUBLISHED SCOPE. The output must state which flows were adjudicated by\ndata flow and which by call reachability alone. A reader must be able to tell\nthe two apart from the emitted record; the scope of data-flow coverage may not\nbe left to assumption.\n\n(b) SANITIZER NEUTRALIZATION. Sanitizers on the path must actually neutralize\nthe taint category in question -- a barrier for a different category must not\nclear the flow.\n\n(c) HONEST LABELLING. Structural (call-graph-only) results must be explicitly\nlabeled approximate.\n\nSUPERSEDES the original clause (a), \"every edge corresponds to actual data\nflow, not just call reachability\", which no conforming implementation could\nsatisfy: ADR-0017 section 7b excludes alias analysis and path sensitivity by\ndesign, and 86.6 percent of the sink catalog is served by call reachability.\nAn invariant that demands completeness from an analysis its own governing\ndocument declares incomplete is a defect in the invariant. Refined by owner\nruling 2026-08-03 over verified evidence, per the standing refined-criterion\npattern (INV-fahub / INV-numat / INV-pubom / D13)."  # 012f
